{
  "id": "chain-011",
  "description": "(0.5.0) Cross-implementation edge vectors (RFC-ACDP-0017 §14). 27 edge cases on which acdp-rs acdp-chain 0.17.1 and acdp-verifier-py (c95cf7b) independently produced byte-identical verdicts at spec 263c3c4. Each pins a bundle, the caller options and the verdict with its digests. A conformant verify_chain MUST reproduce each verdict byte for byte. The cases cover: revocation and discovery-record selection; signature-only, backdated and unreceipted retractions; cycles vs joins; fanout truncation; did:web snapshot selection; tampering, absent vs withheld; event-receipt failures; malformed and unresolvable keys with receipt-attested revocation placement; latest-pass historical event keys; unsigned registry-actor events. The two refusal cases of the same run (max_fanout 101 → invalid_options; a did:key in did_documents → invalid_evidence) also agreed; they remain behavioral in chain-006 D and chain-008 E.",
  "tags": [
    "chain",
    "consumer",
    "offline",
    "0.5.0",
    "known-answer",
    "cross-implementation"
  ],
  "applies_to_profiles": [
    "acdp-consumer-chain"
  ],
  "input": {
    "note": "Each vector's bundle is in examples/evidence/xc-<name>.json and its verdict in examples/chain-verdict/xc-<name>.json. Test keys as chain-001 (_seed_note)."
  },
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "A — reproduce every vector",
      "expected": {
        "behavior": "For each vector, verify_chain(roots, evidence, options) emits the pinned verdict byte for byte under JCS, with the pinned as_of_digest and verdict_digest."
      }
    }
  ],
